    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-12T09:34:07+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T09:34:07+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T23:04:07Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T23:04:07Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough located about northern parts of SA continues crossing the state and will clear to the northeast during the day. A cool southwesterly airstream will follow as a high pressure system drifts eastwards across the Bight early this week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding north of Marla. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 21 to 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy in the morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h turning easterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers in the far west in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
